.TH CONVERT-TO-MP3 1 "May 28, 2026" "convert-to-mp3" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
convert-to-mp3 \- convert video or audio files to MP3 using VLC
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B convert-to-mp3.sh
.RB [ --force | -f ]
.I input-file
.RI [ input-file ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B convert-to-mp3.sh
converts one or more video or audio files to MP3 files using VLC.
.PP
For each input file, the output file is written to the same directory
with the same base name and a
.B .mp3
extension.
.PP
The script uses a 192 kbps MP3 audio stream, 2 channels, and a
44100 Hz sample rate.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR --force , " -f"
Overwrite an existing output MP3 file.
.SH OPERANDS
.TP
.I input-file
A video or audio file to convert. More than one input file may be provided.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Convert one file:
.B ./convert-to-mp3.sh movie.mp4
.TP
Convert multiple files:
.B ./convert-to-mp3.sh movie.mp4 interview.mov audio.wav
.TP
Overwrite existing output files:
.B ./convert-to-mp3.sh --force movie.mp4 interview.mov
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
All files converted successfully.
.TP
.B 1
VLC was not found, a file could not be converted, an output already
existed, or another conversion error occurred.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid usage.
.SH NOTES
When multiple files are provided, per-file errors are reported and the
script continues converting remaining files. If any file fails, the
final exit status is 1.
.PP
VLC is located by checking for
.B cvlc
or
.B vlc
in
.B PATH ,
then by checking the default macOS application path:
.B /Applications/VLC.app/Contents/MacOS/VLC .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR vlc (1)
